    "description": "Level 2: a one-way ring road (six directed segments) with bidirectional spokes to three storage areas and two stations - a realistic anticlockwise traffic scheme. Three units, six pods. Punishes symmetric distance assumptions: getting from a station back to a storage area can cost two thirds of a lap, so unit-to-pod assignment must be computed on directed distances, not undirected ones."
